  "lineage": "Northern Albanian and Kosovar song accompanied by the two-string long-necked çifteli, carried by the Gheg highlands of Malësia and Dukagjin and spread on cassette through the 1970s-90s Kosovo and diaspora market — one string plucked as a fast melodic line, the second sounding a fixed drone, under a nasal declamatory tenor singing strophic heroic and wedding texts in free rhythm or a steady 2/4 with def frame drum",
